ble ref must not advance it. The operation must not repeat staging, reuse its revoked token, replace the original unknown outcome or permit an arbitrary supplied outcome.\n\nDestination 18 has no such act or migration path. Merely adding reservation-stage to recovery.accepts cannot settle this already recorded unknown, and changing a historical pinned definition would break the earlier-pin rule. This needs a protocol and existing-room migration ruling before implementation, rather than a CLI retry. Retaining future own receive-pack replies durably would improve crash recovery, but cannot recover this lost reply or settle this publication by itself.\n\nI continue O2 and the remaining approved queue while that ruling is pending.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}